---
description: seo-audit — v1 scope boundaries and stable contracts
alwaysApply: true
---

**v1 checks only** (don't add more without being asked): title exists/length,
meta description exists/length, exactly one H1, image alt-text coverage,
canonical tag exists, viewport tag exists, duplicate titles across the site,
broken internal links.

**Explicitly deferred — do not implement unless asked:** full schema.org
validation, JS-rendered page auditing, sitemap intelligence, redirect-chain
tracking, orphan-page analysis, duplicate meta-description detection, score
history/trend dashboard, any LLM-based suggestion layer.

**Check interface — all checks implement this, no exceptions:**
```go
type Check interface {
    ID() string
    Name() string
    Run(PageData) CheckResult
}
```

**Exit codes are a stable contract with the CI runner — do not change:**
`0` = passed, `1` = score below `--fail-below` or regression detected,
`2` = crawl/system error.

**JSON report schema is a stable contract with the CI runner.** If a change
seems needed, stop and flag it explicitly rather than silently adding/
renaming/removing fields.

**Baseline storage: file-based, not a database.** The tool reads/writes a
plain JSON report (`<job-dir>/latest.json`) in a persistent directory
provided by the CI runner. Do not add SQLite or any other DB dependency to
this project for baseline storage.
